I wrote the migrated file to `out/module.ts`. The exported signatures (`toSlug`, `byNameKey`, `parseAmount`, `Row`, `Config`) are unchanged.

```ts
import { kebabCase, keyBy } from 'es-toolkit';
import { toNumber } from 'es-toolkit/compat';
// ...
export function toSlug(label: string): string { return kebabCase(label); }
export function byNameKey(rows: Row[]): Record<string, Row> { return keyBy(rows, row => row.name); }
export function parseAmount(text: string): number { return toNumber(text); }
```

| lodash | es-toolkit | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `kebabCase` | `es-toolkit` (strict) | Output matched `es-toolkit/compat` on 14 test strings, including `"Line SIZE_"`, `""`, `a1b` and `XMLHttp2Request`. |
| `keyBy(rows, 'name')` | `es-toolkit` `keyBy` | Strict `keyBy` takes a function, so the adapter is `row => row.name`. When names repeat, the last row wins, as in lodash. |
| `toNumber` | `es-toolkit/compat` | There is no strict version. Compat returned the same as `Number()` on the 13 strings I tried, including `"9x80"`, `"87x47e ."`, `""`, `"0x1f"` and `"+0x1"`. |

I did not compare against real lodash, because it isn't installed in this project. The checks above compare es-toolkit strict against compat, and `toNumber` against `Number()`. No lodash import is kept, since all three functions have an es-toolkit equivalent.

- **Size:** `npm run size -- out/module.ts` reports 346 bytes (min+gzip), with 88 bytes of my own code.
- **Original size:** I couldn't measure `src/module.ts`, since the lodash imports don't resolve here.
- **Type check:** `tsc` reports no errors for `out/module.ts`. The only errors are in the original `src/module.ts`, because lodash isn't installed.

I created `out/module.ts` plus a temporary `out/m2.ts` and scratch test file, which I deleted. I didn't install anything.

